From 7c60aa99f359ea525901372db77cd67d1c9097e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (UI-0.5 assist)" <claude@bytebeam.local>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 20:46:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] UI-0.5: Frontend Foundation Cleanup
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Task 1+3 — Duplicate useApi hook consolidation + centralized API layer:
- Deleted lib/use-api.ts (SWR-based, single consumer: platform-layout.tsx).
- lib/hooks.ts is now the single canonical useApi, used by all 21 pages.
  Interface unchanged for existing 17 callers ({data, loading, error,
  refetch}, deps array) -- zero regression risk, confirmed via repo-wide
  grep of every call site's destructuring pattern before making this
  change.
- Added opt-in third argument (pollInterval) so platform-layout.tsx could
  migrate without losing its 30s-polling behavior, rather than keeping a
  second hook alive just for that one feature.
- Auth-failure handling (auto-logout on 401) moved from the deleted
  use-api.ts into lib/api.ts's request() function -- now applies uniformly
  to every api.* call app-wide (previously only use-api.ts's one consumer
  had this protection). Also more robust: checks the actual HTTP status
  code instead of use-api.ts's prior string-match on the error message.

Task 2 -- Transport consistency (Pricing page):
- Audited: prior UI-0 audit's claim of a 'REST + tRPC mix' on this page
  was incorrect -- verified zero api.get/post calls exist in the file,
  it's pure tRPC. Corrected in the audit doc.
- Decision: KEEP tRPC as-is this phase. A REST equivalent likely exists
  on the backend (pricing-plans.controller.ts confirmed present) but
  migrating this page's create-plan + live-bill-preview logic is real
  page-rewrite work, out of scope for a foundation-cleanup phase that
  explicitly rules out rewriting mature pages. Flagged as a well-scoped
  future task, not executed here.

Task 4 -- Polling strategy:
- Implemented in the consolidated hook (see Task 1): pauses while tab
  hidden, force-refetches on focus/visibility-return. Opt-in, so it only
  changes behavior for platform-layout.tsx's sidebar poll, not any of the
  17 non-polling callers.

Task 5 -- Design token layer (prep only, not applied):
- tailwind.config.ts: added primary/secondary/success/warning/danger/
  surface/background/border/text/muted color tokens, plus radius/spacing/
  shadow tokens. Purely additive -- no existing utility class is touched,
  overridden, or removed, so zero visual regression on any current page.
  Values are not invented: read off the existing slate-950/orange-500
  shell convention and components/ui/badge.tsx's existing variant colors,
  so future token-based components (UI-0.6+) will match what's already
  on screen instead of drifting the way referrals/page.tsx's light theme
  did.

Task 6 -- Documentation:
- Inline comments added at each decision point (why the duplicate hook
  was removed, why tRPC stays, future migration path) rather than a
  separate doc, since these are implementation-level rationale best kept
  next to the code they explain.

Files changed: 5 (4 modified, 1 deleted). Zero touches to Dashboard,
Tenants, Tenant Detail, Feature Flags, Approvals, or Support -- the
'do not touch' list was achievable in full because the consolidated
hook's interface is 100% backward compatible; none of those pages needed
to change to keep working.

Verification note: sandbox cannot run pnpm install / next build here
(same network-restricted limitation as the backend). What was verified
in-sandbox: full repo-wide grep of every useApi call site's exact
destructuring pattern before editing (23 refetch usages, all preserved;
zero refresh/mutate usages, confirmed safe to drop that name); manual
structural review of all edited files. Real build/typecheck/runtime
verification remains a server-side or local-dev step.
